 ## Storage
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+Sessions use a process-local dictionary in [the session store](../../larder/session_store.py), following
+[keep sessions in memory](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-memory.md). The app must create one store at startup and
+reuse it for every request.
+
+## Known limits
+
+- Restarting or deploying the web app loses its sessions; members must log in again and rebuild their pantry orders.
+- Processes do not share sessions. With multiple workers or servers, requests reaching another process cannot find
+  the session. Run a single web process to keep sessions available between requests; this does not preserve them
+  across restarts.
+- Stored entries are not automatically removed. The existing session lifetime calculation is unchanged; reclaiming
+  dictionary memory currently requires restarting the process, which also loses active sessions.
 
 ## Shaped by
 
-- [Keep sessions in the database](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)
